      <div type="clause" n="8">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 8</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="54" ed="#liebermann"/>VIIII. Gif hwa nunnan of mynstere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.6"/> ut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.7"/> álæde butan kyninges lefnesse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.8"/> oððe bisc<hi rend="italic">epes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.9"/></hi>, geselle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.10"/> hundtwelftig scill', healf cyninge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.11"/>, healf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.12"/> biscepe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.13"/> ⁊ þære cirican<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.14"/> hlaforde, ðe ðone munuc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.star"/> age.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="54" ed="#liebermann"/>IX. Gif hwa nunnan of mynstre út alæde buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.1"/> cyninges leafe oððe biscopes, gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.3"/> CXX scill', healf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.5"/> cyninge, healf biscope ⁊ cirican<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.6-2"/> hlaforde, ðe ða<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.7-2"/> nunnan age.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="55" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ða<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe nunnan of mynstre ut alædeð. Gyf hwa nunnan of mynstre ut alǽde butan cyninges leafe oððe bisceopes, gesylle hundtwentig scill', healf cyning<hi rend="italic">e</hi>, healf bisceope, ðære cyrice hlaforde, þe þa nunnan age.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="55" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis sanctimonialem ab ecclesia duxerit sine licentia regis aut episcopi, det centum uiginti solidos, dimidium regi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.5-2"/>, dimidium episcopo et ipsius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_8.lnote.oe.2"/> ecclesie domino, cuius monacha fuit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="68" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ðam þe nunnan of mynstre ut alædeð.] Gif hwa nunnan of mynstere ut álæde butan kyninges lefnesse<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#Af_8.attnote.fn.10"/> oððe biscepes, geselle hundtwelftig<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#Af_8.attnote.fn.11"/> scill', healf cyninge, healf biscepe ⁊ þære cirican hlaforde<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Af_8.attnote.fn.12"/>, ðe ðone munuc<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#Af_8.attnote.fn.13"/> age.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="9" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="302" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{VIIII} Gif hwa nunnan of mynstre ut alæde butan kyninges lefnesse oððe bisc<hi rend="italic">epes</hi>, geselle hundtwelftig scill, healf cyninge, healf biscepe ⁊ þære cirican hlaforde, ðe ðone munuc age.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_8.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="55" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand eine Nonne aus dem Kloster<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_8.lnote.de.2"/> entführt ohne des Königs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_8.lnote.de.3"/> oder des Bischofs Erlaubniss, gebe er 120 Schilling<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_8.lnote.de.4"/>, halb dem König, halb dem Bischof und dem Herrn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_8.lnote.de.5"/> der Kirche<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_8.lnote.de.6"/>, der jene mönchische Person [zur Unterthanin] hat.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone abducts a nun from a minster without the permission of the king or of the bishop, let him give 120 shillings, half to the king, half to the bishop and to the lord of the church who has that monastic person [as subject].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="69" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone takes a nun from a nunnery without the permission of the king or bishop, he shall pay 120 shillings, half to the king, and half to the bishop and<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_8.attnote.n.1"/> the lord of the church, under whose charge the nun<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Af_8.attnote.n.2"/> is.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="411" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone brings a nun out of a nunnery without the permission of the king or the bishop, he is to pay 120 shillings, half to the king and half to the bishop and the lord of the church which has the nun.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="303" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone leads a nun from a minster without the permission of the king or bishop, let him pay one hundred and twenty shillings, half to the king and half to the bishop or the lord of the church that owns the [nun].</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="303"><label>shared vocabulary</label> <ref target="clause:Af_20">Af 20</ref> <quote>This term appears elsewhere only in the Old English translation of Bede's Historia [...] and in §24</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="315"><ref target="clause:Af_20">Af 20</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ster <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> -stre <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ster So; -stre Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">út alæde <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">út alæde Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">lyf. <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> leafe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lyf. So; leafe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ceopes <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ceopes So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gesylle hundtwentig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gesylle hundtwentig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ng <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ng So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">healfe <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">healfe So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ceope <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ceope So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyr. <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> þær cyrice <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyr. So; þær cyrice Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mynecenne <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> ða nunnan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mynecenne So; ða nunnan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">followed by an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Rasur vor</hi> an</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erasure before an</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a nunnan <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a nunnan on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et <hi rend="italic">fügt T zu</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et added by T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Von dem der eine Nonne vom Kloster hinaus entführt’ Rb B</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Of him who abducts a nun out of the convent’ Rb B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Kirche’ Q zu weit. Nicht etwa an eine Stiftsdame ohne Regel und Gelübde (mit Robertson <hi rend="italic">Hist. essays</hi> 174) denke man</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘church’ Q, too broad. One should not think of, say, a canoness without rule or vow (with Robertson <hi rend="italic">Hist. essays</hi> 174)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der König (<hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> 6) erlaubt (und straft unerlaubten) Austritt der Nonne (<hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> 5. 10) aus dem Kloster als Kirchenvogt. Eadgar verkündete Mönchsregel! Vielleicht tritt Af gegen Unzucht der Nonne (<hi rend="italic">s. Gl.</hi> 9d. e) auf infolge der Mahnung durch Papst und Erzbischof von Reims; <hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> S. 34 Sp. 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The king (<hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> 6), as advocate of the church, permits (and punishes when unpermitted) the nun’s departure (<hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> 5. 10) from the convent. Eadgar proclaimed the monastic rule! Perhaps Af is taking action against unchastity of nuns (<hi rend="italic">see Gl.</hi> 9d. e) in consequence of the admonition by the pope and the archbishop of Reims; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> p. 34 col. 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">D. i. ‘Ungehorsam [gegen den König]’; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4. 7. — Das Zahlwort in B ist modernisiert</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">I.e. ‘disobedience [towards the king]’; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4. 7. — The numeral in B is modernised</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Kirchenherr 1. 5; Geistliches Gericht 14. a. Das ‘und’ davor steht wahrscheinlich für ‘oder, beziehungsweise’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Kirchenherr 1. 5; Geistliches Gericht 14. a. The ‘and’ before it probably stands for ‘or, as the case may be’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_8.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">munuc</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi>), auch für ‘Nonne’, nur hier belegt, erschien Abschreibern so seltsam, dass H cor. B ‘Nonne’, So ‘Mönchin’ einsetzten. Doch beliess So den Art. masc. als Rudiment des Authentischen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">munuc</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi>), also used for ‘nun’, attested only here, seemed so strange to copyists that H cor. B substituted ‘nun’, So ‘monkess’. Yet So retained the masc. article as a vestige of the authentic text</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_8.attnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><label>lefnesse</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">leafe</hi>. H &amp; B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_8.attnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><label>hundtwelftig</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hundtwentig</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_8.attnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><label>hlaforde</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">⁊ <hi rend="italic">cirican hlaforde</hi>. H. <hi rend="italic">ðære cyrice hlaforde</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_8.attnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><label>munuc</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þone mynecenne</hi>. So. <hi rend="italic">ða nunnan</hi>. H, B &amp; Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_8.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">It is not certain whether <hi rend="italic">and</hi> should be translated here by ‘or’ or ‘and.’ If it is translated ‘or,’ the <hi rend="italic">hlaford</hi> would, usually at least, be a woman.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_8.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The word <hi rend="italic">munuc</hi> is not elsewhere used for a woman, though <hi rend="italic">munuc had</hi> is used to indicate the monastic life both of men and women (cf. cap. 18, below). H, B, and Ld read <hi rend="italic">þa nunnan</hi>; So, <hi rend="italic">þone mynecenne</hi>. The discrepancy seems to show that <hi rend="italic">þone munuc</hi> was the original reading and was not understood by later scribes.</seg></note>
      </div>
